sources:
    - id: cdm2008
      title: 'The Impact of Nearly Universal Insurance Coverage on Health Care Utilization: Evidence from Medicare'
      authors: David Card, Carlos Dobkin, Nicole Maestas, American Economic Review 98(5)
      year: 2008
      finding: 'NHIS 1999-2003: the share with any health insurance is 87.9% at ages 63-64 and jumps by 9.5 percentage points (SE 0.6) at 65; background characteristics such as employment, marriage and poverty change little at 65. Hospital admissions (CA, FL, NY discharge records 1992-2002) rise 7.6% (SE 0.3) at 65.'
      doi: 10.1257/aer.98.5.2242

