audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    'female|a||In America, your sixty-fifth birthday changes almost nothing about you, except your health insurance: Medicare starts, for almost everyone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So can that one day tell us whether health insurance keeps people alive?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:149u5cj'
    female|a||The obvious test compares people old enough for Medicare, say at seventy, with people too young for it, say at sixty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nty054'
    female|a||But a seventy-year-old is ten years older, and age alone raises the risk of dying.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:winbdd'
    female|a||Before we go on, your pick. Which comparison would isolate what Medicare does?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:c9n72x'
    'female|a||A month either side of sixty-five: the two groups are the same age in every way that matters, and only one of them has Medicare.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||So shrink the age gap until ageing can''t matter: a month short of sixty-five against a month past it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||First, though, the birthday has to change something. Up the side, the share of Americans with any health insurance.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jo8n4j'
    female|a||At sixty-three and sixty-four, about eighty-eight in a hundred are covered.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:16ccc4d'
    female|a||Then the line breaks. Just past sixty-five, coverage jumps by about nine and a half percentage points.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2c3a67'
    female|a||Card, Dobkin and Maestas measured that jump in national health surveys from 1999 to 2003, with a standard error of just over half a point.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:trkns3'
    female|a||Income, marriage and work, meanwhile, pass through sixty-five with barely a ripple.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:zi9y6m'
    female|a||Nothing about a person changes overnight at sixty-five. A legal rule does, and nobody can choose which side of their own birthday they are on.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6aq6d9'
    female|a||A design built on a cutoff like that is called a regression discontinuity, and age, the number the rule reads, is its running variable.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gtuinn'
    female|a||If coverage jumps at the line and nothing else does, then a jump in health at the line points to Medicare.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:13k51z4'
    female|a||That 'nothing else' is the whole design, so it needs stating exactly.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:a4w13j'
    female|a||To see what has to be true at that line, take one kind of patient, with round numbers of our own, close to the real ones.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||They arrive at an emergency room with a heart attack or a stroke, and we count who dies within a week.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:whhfjh'
    'female|a||The red line is each age''s death rate without Medicare, Y-zero: five in a hundred at sixty-five, creeping up with age.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1niin2h'
    female|a||The blue line is the same patients with Medicare, Y-one. Say it sits one point lower at every age.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:aibc0a'
    'female|a||But each age shows us only one of them: the red line before the birthday, the blue line after.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:183s6yl'
    'female|a||So what we actually see is red up to sixty-five, then blue: five in a hundred, then four.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ur5ldu'
    'female|a||That step down of one point is the gap between the two lines at exactly sixty-five: the effect of becoming eligible for Medicare, at that age.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:eod065'
    female|a||Everyone crosses into eligibility on the same birthday, which makes this a sharp design.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mfnjgc'
    female|a||And it is that gap only if the red line, the one we stop seeing, would have carried straight on through the birthday.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1v0bcii'
    'female|a||That is the assumption the whole design rests on, called continuity: without Medicare, the average death rate would not jump at sixty-five, and the same holds for the death rate with it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:r64lnx'
    female|a||Now suppose something else also happened at sixty-five, say many people retired that day and retiring changed their health. That would lift both lines past the birthday, so the blue line we see rises too.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:cdvckg'
    'female|a||Watch the red line lift past sixty-five: the step seen shrinks, while Medicare''s effect stays at minus one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lum6qs'
    female|a||Lift it six tenths of a point, and the step we see shrinks to minus zero point four, though Medicare's own effect never moved from minus one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So anything else that changes at sixty-five lands inside the estimate. That is why the smooth income, marriage and work matter.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1czvput'
    female|a||A new case to try. Suppose a state also gave everyone a free yearly check-up from their 65th birthday on. What would the step at 65 measure?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jwqfcd'
    'female|a||Both together: the check-ups start at the same line, so the red line would jump on its own, and continuity fails for Medicare alone.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Still, this asks less than comparing how two groups change over time, which needs them to move in parallel for years: here, nothing may break at one single point.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||The price is reach. The step tells us about people at sixty-five, not at fifty, and not at eighty.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kup1k6'
    female|a||And real data never hand us these clean lines. They hand us noisy points, and the step has to be read from them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7h9r2y'
    'female|a||Here is what real data look like: points, one for each narrow band of ages.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Card, Dobkin and Maestas gathered about four hundred thousand emergency admissions in California hospitals, from 1992 to 2002.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:5sghka'
    female|a||Each point is the share of patients of one age who died within a week. These points come from our round numbers; theirs look much the same.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:124msik'
    female|a||To read the step, fit a line to each side separately, using only ages near the birthday. They used sixty to seventy, with a gentle curve on each side.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10rv81r'
    female|a||Then read the gap where the two fitted lines meet the cutoff.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4bjmfy'
    'female|a||Their own estimate, from the real data: one point one percentage points fewer deaths within a week, with a standard error of zero point two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1rvuflu'
    female|a||Just under sixty-five, about five in a hundred of these patients died within a week, so that is roughly one death in five prevented.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1y05aw1'
    female|a||And the gap had not closed nine months later.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17tin50'
    female|a||But the choice that mattered most in this study was not the line fitting. It was which patients to count.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1j8unop'
    female|a||At sixty-five there are about seven and a half percent more hospital admissions overall, with a standard error of zero point three, in records from California, Florida and New York.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dsk14u'
    female|a||Think about who walks in. Suppose Medicare also brought milder cases into hospital after 65. Which way would that push the measured step in deaths?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ub3em'
    'female|a||Toward fewer deaths: milder patients die less often, so adding them after sixty-five would make Medicare look better than it is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||So they kept only conditions that cannot wait: ones admitted as often on a Sunday as on a Monday, such as heart attacks and strokes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||For those, the number of patients arriving runs smoothly through sixty-five, so both sides hold the same mix of the very sick.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ssxe4w'
    'female|a||And their insurance did change: Medicare as the main payer rose by about forty-four points, and the uninsured share fell by about seven points, from about one in ten.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1v42coq'
    female|a||With it came a few more procedures, and hospital bills about three percent higher.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:we8hxa'
    female|a||So who exactly did Medicare save? Most of these patients had insurance before sixty-five, too.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Only about seven in a hundred went from no insurance to some at the birthday.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1u447be'
    female|a||Yet deaths within a week fell by about one point one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ss45pt'
    female|a||And by the authors' own count, about five in a hundred uninsured patients just under sixty-five died within a week.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:117y43o'
    female|a||Try the bound yourself. If coverage had saved every one of those newly insured patients, how much of the drop of 1.1 points could that explain?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:v5gs09'
    'female|a||At most about 0.4 points: five in a hundred of about seven in a hundred, roughly a third of the drop.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Seven in a hundred, times five in a hundred, is at most about zero point four points, even if coverage saved every one of them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||So most of the gain went to patients who were insured already: something about Medicare changed how they were treated.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:114vy89'
    female|a||Which part did it, the data cannot say. For the already insured the kind of insurance changes, hospitals are paid differently, and retirement and Social Security cluster near sixty-five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gzpix1'
    female|a||Effects split by insurance before sixty-five, and by what hospitals did, would tell those apart. The authors found more care inside the same hospitals, not moves to better ones.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1hpom59'
    'female|a||That is also why dividing by the jump in coverage, as a fuzzy design would, misleads here: it assumes Medicare works only through the newly insured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:j8rcf9'
    female|a||Minus one point one over seven point four points is about fifteen points per newly insured patient, impossible when only five in a hundred die, as the bound just showed.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:h1xn6w'
    female|a||Nor does this step speak for people of forty. For them it takes another source, such as Oregon's 2008 lottery, which drew names for Medicaid among low-income adults.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1102eee'
    'female|a||And before trusting any step, researchers stress-test it: other windows, other curve shapes, and checks that nobody sorts to one side of the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1bems6o'
    'female|a||So, can one birthday tell us whether insurance keeps people alive? For very sick patients at sixty-five, it can: about one death in five within a week was avoided.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1bvy8ba'
    female|a||It works because the rule jumps and, as far as anyone can check, nothing else does. That is continuity, and it stays an assumption.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:18b8jao'
    'female|a||And the answer belongs to the line: people at sixty-five, in California hospitals, in the 1990s.':
